  "rationale": "Evidence: iteration 3 (kp 2.5, sensor 0.016) scored 159.2, the best raced score. Every run still ended off_track. max_error stayed at 0.061 (oval), 0.062 (s-bend) and 0.062 (slalom), so it did not fall below the 0.06 m limit. Line-loss events rose on the s-bend from 1.15 to 2.0 when kp went from 2.0 to 2.5, and the slalom stayed at 1.0. The s-bend max_error also worsened slightly (0.0616 to 0.0623). That suggests that raising steering authority alone is not fixing the bend excursions, and that the line is being lost during them. steering_oscillation (0.14 to 0.28) is still low, so kd 0.3 and kp 2.5 leave room. The 16 mm footprint is already at its maximum, so line loss must be addressed through controller.line_loss. Change: controller.line_loss from last_direction to search_right, the only change. kp stays 2.5, base_speed 1.3, kd 0.3, ki 0.05, weights [2,1,0,-1,-2], sensor_size 0.016. Expected result: line_loss_events on the s-bend and slalom fall toward 1 or less, and max_error drops slightly, so more runs survive the bends. Hypotheses and next measurements: (1) if line_loss_events do not fall with search_right, the loss is caused by steering overshoot, not by the recovery direction; then return to last_direction and test kp 3.0 alone. (2) If max_error falls below about 0.058 m while completion_time is above 3 s, raise base_speed from 1.3 to 1.5. (3) If the oval finishes increase, the kp 2.5 gain is adequate for that track. I need per-track max_error, line_loss_events, progress, completion_time and steering_oscillation.",
